{"name":"Uptown Girl","hex":"#a791a8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"uptown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The residential part of a city, which is usually away from the central business district.","The commercial center of town (in Charlotte, North Carolina)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["In the upper part of a town.","Of or relating to an affluent area or population."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uptown"},{"term":"girl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female child.","A woman, especially a young and often attractive woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feminize or girlify; to gender as a girl or as for girls.","To staff with or as a girl or girls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Uptown Girl","blocks":[{"text":"\"Uptown Girl\" is a song written and performed by American musician Billy Joel from his ninth studio album, An Innocent Man (1983), released in September 1983 as the album's second single. The lyrics describe a working-class \"downtown man\" attempting to woo a wealthy \"uptown girl\".\nThe 12\" EP has the tracks \"My Life\", \"Just the Way You Are\" and \"It's Still Rock and Roll to Me\", whereas some 7\" single versions featured \"Careless Talk\" as a B-side."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Uptown_Girl_joel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uptown_Girl"},{"title":"Uptown Girl (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Uptown Girl is the first extended play of South Korean rapper Mirani. It was released on November 30, 2021, through At Area."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Mirani_Uptown_Girl_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uptown_Girl_(EP)"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Christie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christie Brinkley, Joel's future wife, appears as the main character of the video","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChristie_Brinkley_by_David_Shankbone_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9a/9UptownGirl1.jpg/330px-9UptownGirl1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9a/9UptownGirl1.jpg/330px-9UptownGirl1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A9UptownGirl1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c